 ### HeadNeRF Volume Rendering
-HeadNeRF computes a low-resolution 2D feature map $I_F$ from ray samples to serve as input for a subsequent 2D neural rendering module [S5]. It samples 64 points per ray [S5]. The output feature map $I_F$ dimensions are $R^{256 \times 32 \times 32}$ [S5]. Hierarchical volume sampling is removed to speed up inference, accepting potential quality trade-offs for real-time performance [S5].
