 ### NeRSTF Rendering
-NeRSTF combines Signed Distance Fields (SDF) and Texture Fields (TF) or a combined NeRSTF model, using a two-pass rendering approach (coarse stratified, fine importance) to produce backpropagable views [S7, unofficial]. Steps: 1. Query the model (sdf/tf or nerstf) for density, signed distance, and channels at query points. 2. Render rays with coarse, stratified samples using StratifiedRaySampler. 3. Render rays with fine, importance-weighted samples using the sampler from the coarse pass. 4. Scale output channels by channel_scale (default 255.0). 5. If separate_shared_samples is true, include coarse results in the output dictionary [S7, unofficial]. Parameters: n_coarse_samples, n_fine_samples, separate_shared_samples [S7, unofficial].
